      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "sce:cc-tou-d-4-9pm-2026-03-20",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "sce:cc-tou-d-4-9pm-2026-03-20-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "Three things published for Option 4-9 PM are not represented in this filing. First, the Baseline Credit of $(0.10108) per kWh: the rate sheet footnote states that it applies up to 100 percent of the Baseline Allocation, with additional allocations for customers who have a Heat Pump Water Heater, the allocations being set out in Preliminary Statement Part H. The filing carries the credit as an unbounded per-kilowatt-hour amount with no allocation quantity attached, so a consumer computing a bill will credit every kilowatt-hour rather than only those within baseline, overstating the credit for a customer above baseline. Second, the Option 4-9 PM-CPP variant printed on the same Sheet 2: a CPP Event Energy Charge of $0.80000 per kWh, a Summer on-peak non-event energy credit of $(0.15170) per kWh, and a Summer Season Maximum Available Credit of $(0.58794) per kWh, none of them modeled. Third, the two pilot bill discounts in Special Conditions 15 and 16: the San Joaquin Valley Disadvantaged Communities Pilot Bill Protection Discount (20 percent in years 1 through 5, then 10 or 20 percent in years 6 through 10) and the 20 percent Transitional Community Solar Discount. Several Special Conditions are out of scope rather than missing: the twelve-month rate change restriction in Special Condition 7, the Arrearage Management Plan debt forgiveness in Special Condition 10, and the Discontinued TOU Period provisions of Special Condition 14, whose own terms expired for all customers on July 31, 2022, govern account administration rather than price. The Deed Restricted Base Services Charge adjustment of $(0.332) per meter per day and the CARE and FERA discount lines are cross-references to separate schedules, each filed as its own modifier in this corpus.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-09-21T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
